hadiths[31]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7570","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ziyad bin Al-Khalil Al-Tustari told us, Abdul Rahman bin Al-Mubarak told us, Hammad bin Zaid told us, On the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man laid down a sheep that he wanted to slaughter while he was sharpening his razor, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Do you want to cause her to die? “Did you mark your labia before you had sex with her?” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7570 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7571","Amr bin Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Adl told us, Al-Sari bin Khuzaymah told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them, who said: God, Blessed and Most High, says: {Mention the name of God over it with rows} He said: “Standing up on three reasonable lists, in the name of God, and God is greater, O God, from you and to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7571 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7572","Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Qantari told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, On the authority of Jabir bin Zayd and Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, regarding a man who slaughtered and forgot to say the name. He said: “He eats.” And on the Magi. He slaughters and says the name of God. He said: “Do not eat.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7572 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7573","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Anazi told me, Muadh bin Najd Al-Qurashi told us, Qubaisa bin Uqba told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Waki’, who is Harun bin Antara, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, in the words of God Almighty: {And They ate of that over which the name of God was not mentioned.} [Al-An’am: 121] He said: “The polytheists disputed with them and said: What they killed, they ate, and what God killed, they did not eat.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7573 - True"
"7574","Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Ibn Abi Omar told us, Sufyan told us, Amr bin Dinar told us, he said: I heard Suhaib, the client of Ibn Amir, narrates that Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, told him on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no A person kills a bird or something above it without its right, but God Almighty will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is her right? He said: “Her right is for him to slaughter it and eat it, and not to cut off its head and throw it away.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7574 - True"
"7575","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr saying: I passed with Ibn Umar on one of the roads of Medina, and behold, a young man had They set up a chicken and threw it. He said: Then he got angry and said: “Who did this?” So they dispersed, and Ibn Umar said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed whoever mutilates an animal.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and it was not They bring it out in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7575 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7576","Muhammad bin Yazid al-Adl told me, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Hilal bin Bishr told us, Abu Khalaf Abdullah bin Issa told us. Al-Khazzaz, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to my father Al-Haytham bin Al-Tayhan: “Beware of milk. Sacrifice for us a young female.” So Abu Al-Haytham ordered his wife, and she kneaded dough for them, and Abu Al-Haytham cut it. Meat, cooking and grilling “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7576 - True"
"7577","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid bin Musa told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Habib told us, on the authority of Nawfal Ibn Abd al-Malik, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He forbade the slaughter of women of pearls and Settlement of the commodity before sunrise.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7577 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7578","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Bishr bin Bakr told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Hassan bin Attiya, Abu Kabsha Al-Saluli told me, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Forty qualities, the highest of which is the gift of a goat. No servant should work with any of them in the hope of its reward and the fulfillment of its promise except “God admitted him into Paradise with it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take him out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7578 - True"
"7579","Abu Aoun Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahan al-Khazzaz informed us, in Mecca at al-Safa, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Hajjaj ibn Minhaal, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his companions They passed by a woman and she slaughtered a sheep for them and prepared food for them. When he returned, she said: O Messenger of God, we have prepared food for you, so go in. So they ate, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his companions entered, and they were not starting until the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began, so he took a morsel and did not eat. He is able to make her happy. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “This is a sheep that was slaughtered without the permission of its owner.” The woman said: O Prophet of God. We are not modest with the family of Muadh, and they are not modest with us. We take from them and they take from us. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7579 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7580","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, and Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them, “They were slaughtered on the day of Khaybar.” Donkeys, mules, and horses, but the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade them from donkeys and mules, but did not forbid them from horses. This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7580 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7581","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl informed us, Yahya bin Abi Talib informed us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Ata informed us, Dawud bin Abi informed us Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Safwan, that he had two rabbits and could not find any iron to slaughter them, so he slaughtered them with a blade, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, I hunted two rabbits and did not find any iron to slaughter them, so I slaughtered them with a crowbar. Should I eat? He said: “Yes, all.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, although there is a difference of opinion regarding it according to Al-Sha’bi, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7581 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7582","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul-Wahhab told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Nabesha, May God be pleased with him. He said: A man asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, we used to observe a period of mourning in pre-Islamic times, and from Rajab, what Do you command us? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Sacrifice to God in whatever month it is, and be righteous to God and feed.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration and did not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7582 - True"
"7583","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Al-Faraj told us, Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Hafsa bint Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded in “The branch in every five is one” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7583 - True"
"7584","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Al-Fadl Al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah Al-Hazami told us, Dawud bin Qays told us. Al-Farra’, he said: I heard Amr bin Shuaib speaking on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked Concerning the branch, he said: “The branch is a right, but if you leave it until it is the son of Makhad or the son of milk, then you burden him for the sake of God or give him to a widow.” “It is better than slaughtering it with its meat stuck to its hair and leaving it as your she-camel.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7584 - True"
"7585","And Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abdul Razzaq told us, he told us Ibn Jurayj, Amr ibn Dinar told me, that Ibn Abi Ammar told him on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him. He said in Al-Far’ah: “It is true. And do not slaughter it while it is a lump of glue sticking to your hand, but fill it with milk, so if it is of the wealth of choice, then slaughter it.” This “An authentic hadith with this chain of transmission, and the hadith transmitted before this one is authentic according to what I stipulated for this book.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7585 - True"
"7586","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, and Ishaq bin Al-Hussein Al-Harbi told us, they said: We told us: Affan bin Muslim, Yahya bin Zurarah bin Karim Al-Sahmi told us, my father told me, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Harith bin Amr Al-Sahmi, may God be pleased with him. He said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: Ask forgiveness for me. He said: “May God forgive you.” I told him that once or twice, and a man said: O Messenger of God, what do you think of the sins and far-fetches? Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever wishes may leave, and whoever wishes may not leave, and whoever wishes may leave, and whoever wishes may not leave, and the sheep must be sacrificed.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, for Al-Harith bin Amr Al-Sahmi is a famous companion, and his children in Basra are famous. “Abdullah narrated Al-Rahman bin Mahdi bin Qutayba, and others, on the authority of Yahya bin Zurarah, “The two sheikhs, may God be pleased with them, agreed on Saeed Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Neither Far’ nor Ataira.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7586 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7587","Al-Hussein bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The boy is a mortgagee. His aqeeqah shall be slaughtered for him on the seventh day, and his head shall be shaved, and it shall be called the seventh day.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7587 - True"
"7588","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Abdullah bin Wahb, Muhammad bin Amr told me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pardoned Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein on the seventh day, named them, and ordered that harm be removed from their heads.” This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it in this context, and this Muhammad bin Amr is: Al-Yafi’i, but I combined Al-Rabi’ and Ibn Abd. “Al-Hakam”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7588 - True"
"7589","Abu Al-Tayyib Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hairi told us, from the origin of his book, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra told us, Ya’la bin Ubaid, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali bin Abu Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cut off a sheep on behalf of Hussein and said: “O Fatima, shave his head and give alms.” As much as the weight of his hair.” So we weighed it, and its weight was one dirham.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7589 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7590","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrafi told me about Marw, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Attab Sahl bin Hamshadh told us, Sawwar Abu told us Hamza, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed aqāt on behalf of Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, on the authority of each one of them.” “Two rams of equal size.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7590 - Abu Hamza’s bracelet is weak"
"7591","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, my father told me, on the authority of Siba’ bin Thabit, on the authority of Umm Karaz, may God be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Put the birds on their perches.”
And I heard him say: “Two sheep for the boy and two sheep for the girl, and it does not harm you, male or female.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7591 - True"
"7592","Ismail bin Al-Fadl told me, my grandfather told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah Al-Hazami told us, Dawud bin Qays told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the aqiqah, and he said: “I do not like to be unobligated by someone born to him.” There is a child among you, and he would like to be kept away from it, so let him do two sheep for the boy and two sheep for the girl.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and it is not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7592 - True"
"7593","Abu Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saying: “Indeed, the boy has an aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf and pour “The harm caused to him.” Jarir said: Al-Hasan was asked about the harm? He said: “It is poetry.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7593 - True"
"7594","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Ibrahim bin Hilal told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, Abd told us Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: “In pre-Islamic times, when a boy was born to us, we would slaughter a sheep for him, shave his head, and smear his With her blood, when Islam was established, when a boy was born to us, we would slaughter a sheep for him, shave his head, and smear his head with saffron.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7594 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7595","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani informed us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah told us, Yazid bin Harun informed us, Abdullah informed us Al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Umm Karaz and Abu Karaz, who said: A woman from the family of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr vowed that Abdul Rahman’s wife gave birth to Naharna Jazar, and Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “No, in fact, the Sunnah is better than the boy, two sheep.” Two equivalents, and on behalf of a female slave, a sheep is cut at a long time without a bone being broken, so it may be eaten and fed and given in charity, and that should be on the seventh day. “If it is not, then on the fourteenth, and if it is not, then on the twenty-one.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7595 - True"
"7596","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Asim told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Qais, he said: A boy was born to me, and I was given the good news about him while I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: I would like for you a piece of bread and meat in his place. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you say that, they are stingy, cowardly, and sad, but they are the fruit of hearts and the joy of the eye.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7596 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7597","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub, Bakkar bin Qutayba told us, Abu Dawud told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Dinar told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Waqid Al-Laythi, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is “Dead.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7597 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7598","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He was asked about the burden of camel humps and sheep’s horseshoes, and he said: “Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7598 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7599","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told me, Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Najia told us, Uthman bin Abi Shaybah told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, Al-Hasan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Masoud, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: We were with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and we passed a tree in which were two red chicks, so we took them. He said: Then the red chick came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She was screaming, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who made this woman fall ill with her two chicks?” He said: So we said: We. He said: “They sent them back.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not take it out.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7599 - True"
"7600","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Murri bin Qatari, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, we are hunting and we do not find a knife except a knife and the end of a stick. He said: “Blood as you wish, and mention the name of God Almighty.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not narrated by “the last book of sacrifices.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7600 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
